# Architecture document

## Canonical docs

- Living architecture: [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Feature map (domains, relationships, UI ↔ API): [`docs/TECHNICAL_FEATURES.md`](docs/TECHNICAL_FEATURES.md)

## When to update (same change set as the code)

Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when the work:

- Adds, changes, or removes **user-visible behavior** (pages, flows, permissions, copy that reflects behavior), or
- Adds, changes, or removes an **HTTP API** (Route Handlers under `src/app/api/`, request/response shape, status codes, auth requirements, redirects).

For the same change set, update `docs/TECHNICAL_FEATURES.md` when you introduce or materially change a **domain capability** or **cross-entity flow** (new subsystem, new way two features connect, or a new primary UI ↔ API pairing). For small fixes, a one-line change log entry in `TECHNICAL_FEATURES.md` is enough.

**Skip** updates for typo-only, formatting-only, comment-only, or internal refactors with **no** API or user-visible impact.

## What to change in the doc

- Edit the **smallest relevant sections** (Overview, Tech stack, Repository map, Runtime boundaries, API surface, Data model, Cross-cutting concerns).
- In `TECHNICAL_FEATURES.md`, adjust the relevant **Domain** subsection, diagrams/tables if the mental model shifted, and **Change log (technical features)**.
- Add a bullet under **Change log (architecture)** with the date, a one-line summary, and which sections you touched.
- Prefer **paths and short descriptions** over large code blocks. Link to handlers or entities instead of pasting implementations.

## If unsure

Default to a **short note** in the appropriate section plus a **change log** line so the doc stays honest without over-documenting internals.
